<p>Yasser Abbas, the 64-year-old son of Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas, won a seat on Fatah’s Central Committee in elections at the movement’s first general conference in almost a decade, a party official said Sunday. Mahmoud Abbas, 90, will remain Fatah chairman after the conference, which also renewed the party’s leadership. Preliminary results showed jailed Fatah leader Marwan Barghouti leading the vote, while Majed Faraj, head of Palestinian General Intelligence and a close Abbas ally, placed second ahead of Jibril Rajoub, according to early results cited by The New Arab. Yasser Abbas, a businessman who spends much of his time in Canada, entered formal politics about five years ago when he was appointed his father’s special representative, AFP reported. The Palestinian Authority has faced pressure to hold long-delayed presidential and parliamentary elections. The conference was Fatah’s first in almost a decade and followed the Gaza war.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/MvtEr1IJ5zEX8d9rTKxJG7j0I7JDW9jVkPiHqHncim2updUvBxGznJcwHq2uV3yk2uwibhfO6n-0HjImApo_kCWhBbm3qRRqN7sN1e5E7AzC4x3Q4XL5E1NaZBmTX2DMsCaDJCU9TyrH79VCEiqBeFywJwND9iluhMv_xPVkGmq3xqGFUYtKAmhx93tj3X2jp_P6hJBKr3FbWbIiACswtiiV6cfe3cmJvbvQ_A4uaZX88eG4Kh8Mjg4C9jk23Q7GFxp1Q4A0hrGIwyH9QaNV' alt='Yasser Abbas, son of Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas, before the Fatah leadership vote.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Vote numbers: Fatah’s Central Committee contest drew 2,507 voters, a 94.64% turnout, and 59 candidates competed for 18 seats, according to figures cited by JNS.</li><li>Council race: Counting continued Sunday in a separate race in which 450 candidates competed for 80 seats on the Revolutionary Council, Fatah’s internal parliament.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Fatah critics of Yasser Abbas: Some officials quoted in the Reuters report said Mahmoud Abbas may be positioning Yasser Abbas for a future leadership role and questioned his ability to bridge Palestinian divisions. (<a href='https://www.algemeiner.com/2026/05/17/palestinian-leaders-son-wins-role-in-abbas-party-official-says/'>Algemeiner</a>)</li><li>Palestinian analysts cited by The New Arab: The analysts described Marwan Barghouti as a figure who could help unite Fatah and Hamas and rebuild a wider Palestinian political consensus. (<a href='https://www.newarab.com/news/marwan-barghouti-tops-fatah-vote-succession-questions-grow'>The New Arab</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/palestinian-leaders-son-wins-role-in-abbas-party-official-says/article70991196.ece'>Palestinian leader&#x27;s son wins role in Abbas&#x27; party, official says</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260517-palestinian-president-s-son-yasser-abbas-elected-to-top-fatah-post'>Palestinian president’s son Yasser Abbas elected to top Fatah post</a> - france24.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/palestinian-presidents-son-elected-to-top-fatah-leadership-body'>Palestinian president’s son elected to top Fatah leadership body</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.newarab.com/news/marwan-barghouti-tops-fatah-vote-succession-questions-grow'>Marwan Barghouti tops Fatah vote as succession questions grow</a> - newarab.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/palestinian-presidents-son-elected-top-fatah-leadership-body'>Palestinian president&#x27;s son elected to top Fatah leadership body</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/17/son-of-palestinian-president-mahmoud-abbas-elected-to-top-fatah-body'>Son of Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas elected to top Fatah body</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://english.aawsat.com/node/5274089'>Palestinian President&#x27;s Son Elected to Top Fatah Leadership Body</a> - aawsat.com</li><li><a href='https://www.leparisien.fr/international/israel/autorite-palestinienne-le-fils-d